  year    = {2009},
  doi     = {10.1016/j.anbehav.2009.01.028},
  note    = {Pagurus bernhardus, shocked inside the shell. Only shocked crabs evacuated, and fewer evacuated from a preferred species of shell than from an unpreferred one, which is the motivational trade-off the book cites: the noxious signal is weighed against the value of the shell rather than triggering a fixed response. Agent-verified 2026-09-18. The authors' own conclusion goes further, that the results are consistent with pain in these animals, and that further step is disputed -- Diggles, Review of Some Scientific Issues Related to Crustacean Welfare, ICES Journal of Marine Science 76(1) (2019): 66--81, argues specifically that shell evacuation does not evidence pain and that the evidential bar has been set too low. The book's sentence claims the trade-off and not the pain, so it does not rest on the disputed step.}
}

